{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851393-what-is-the-solar-advantage-in-3ed","id":851393,"title":"What is the Solar advantage in 3ed?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-22T15:30:11-07:00","id":851393,"title":"What is the Solar advantage in 3ed?","content":"So I have been looking at forums recently and it occurs to me that I don't see the advantage of Solars in 3ed... I am going to list my reasons for this assumptions in the hopes that someone can point out the mistake in my reasoning. I am generally trying to figure out why the other Exalted would serve the Solars in the First Age if they were not particularly powerful.<br /> -Sorcery does not really seem to be it anymore as it requires essence 5 which was supposedly absurdly rare even in the First Age now...<br /> -Evocations might be it but details are so scarce on them that I don't quite know how to define the Solar 'mastery' other than the ability to use several materials (given the required commitment that seems pretty trivial).<br /> -I have seen the opinion many times that a combat-spec'd Full Moon can defeat a combat-spec'd Dawn on the forums.<br /> -Solar's CAN use SMA but they cannot eclipse (no pun intended) Sidereal mastery.<br /> So that really only leaves Supernals (dubious considering that a Solar will face a near-universal disadvantage in terms of combat experience (not XP), Wyld-shaping and crafting as the main Solar advantages I see left...<br /> So ya I would appreciate it if someone could clear up where I am getting it wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T15:33:05-07:00","id":851394,"title":"","content":"Better charms. That was always the main advantage of Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T15:33:48-07:00","id":851395,"title":"","content":"They're better at being successful. That's usually considered a significant advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T15:36:51-07:00","id":851396,"title":"","content":"IMO? Charm power and cost-efficiency of effects. Which is hard to assert as the overwhelming advantage when we don't have many examples of other splats' Charms. But it seems like this must be the clear thing.<br /> <br /> Supernal and MA Mastery effects (which Solars get easily, while Sidereals may not get so easily) is a factor in this, but we also don't know what Supernal effects other splats may have either. Also the capability of more powerful Sorcerous Workings, with Charms that enhance your ability to do them.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851393-what-is-the-solar-advantage-in-3ed#post851393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-I have seen the opinion many times that a combat-spec'd Full Moon can defeat a combat-spec'd Dawn on the forums.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Can&quot; also doesn't mean &quot;always will.&quot; In 2e, it was basically &quot;Solaroids will always win vs other Exalts, given stunts to regen resources, because their defenses are per se better and cheaper (and barring being grappled).&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Can&quot; is simply &quot;can.&quot; In 100 white room scenarios, I doubt the Full Moon would win every time. Maybe half? It depends on a lot of variables, not the least being Charms available, gear, and dice statistics. <br /> <br /> And again, we don't know what the full scope of the Lunar combat trees looks like, so we have only a very vague idea of what a combat-specced Full Moon would look like on paper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T15:39:19-07:00","id":851397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851393-what-is-the-solar-advantage-in-3ed?p=851396#post851396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO? Charm power and cost-efficiency of effects. Which is hard to assert as the overwhelming advantage when we don't have many examples of other splats' Charms. But it seems like this must be the clear thing.<br /> <br /> Supernal and MA Mastery effects (which Solars get easily, while Sidereals may not get so easily) is a factor in this, but we also don't know what Supernal effects other splats may have either. Also the capability of more powerful Sorcerous Workings, with Charms that enhance your ability to do them.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> &quot;Can&quot; also doesn't mean &quot;always will.&quot; In 2e, it was basically &quot;Solaroids will always win vs other Exalts, given stunts to regen resources, because their defenses are per se better and cheaper (and barring being grappled).&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Can&quot; is simply &quot;can.&quot; In 100 white room scenarios, I doubt the Full Moon would win every time. Maybe half? It depends on a lot of variables, not the least being Charms available, gear, and dice statistics.<br /> <br /> And again, we don't know what the full scope of the Lunar combat trees looks like, so we have only a very vague idea of what a combat-specced Full Moon would look like on paper.</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify I meant mostly from a fluff perspective (but that does answer my questions i terms of mechanics.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T15:43:22-07:00","id":851401,"title":"","content":"- Sorcery doesn't require E5. I have no idea where you got that idea from. Sorcery works on a starting character, and sorcerous workings are very powerful. Solars are the masters of sorcery.<br /> - Solar charms are more efficient when it comes to motes spending than other Exalts.<br /> - Details on evocations aren't scarce. They provide a way for Solars to gain access to abilities outside of their niche.<br /> - SMAs aren't better than CMAs. They're just more... esoteric?<br /> - I haven't seen any comments about full moons vs solars in third edition. Not sure where you got that from.<br /> <br /> Solars ruled because Solars were empowered by the king of the heavens and given the authority to rule. Lunars and Sidereals were partners. Sort of like Batman and Wonder Woman aren't Superman's servants, even if he's the leader.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T15:45:19-07:00","id":851406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851393-what-is-the-solar-advantage-in-3ed?p=851401#post851401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Sorcery doesn't require E5. I have no idea where you got that idea from. Sorcery works on a starting character, and sorcerous workings are very powerful. Solars are the masters of sorcery.<br /> - Solar charms are more efficient when it comes to motes spending than other Exalts.<br /> - Details on evocations aren't scarce. They provide a way for Solars to gain access to abilities outside of their niche.<br /> - SMAs aren't better than CMAs. They're just more... esoteric?<br /> - I haven't seen any comments about full moons vs solars in third edition. Not sure where you got that from.<br /> <br /> Solars ruled because Solars were empowered by the king of the heavens and given the authority to rule. Lunars and Sidereals were partners. Sort of like Batman and Wonder Woman aren't Superman's servants, even if he's the leader.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the Core specifically said that Celestial and Solar circles could not be achieved using Supernal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T15:47:57-07:00","id":851409,"title":"","content":"CCS and SCS aren't the be-all end-all. Nor are they required for more powerful Workings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T15:54:58-07:00","id":851413,"title":"","content":"I expect Solar XP will be a factor. I presume that if everyone had exactly the same thing with the same mechanics, they would have called it something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T16:06:03-07:00","id":851422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851393-what-is-the-solar-advantage-in-3ed?p=851413#post851413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I expect Solar XP will be a factor. I presume that if everyone had exactly the same thing with the same mechanics, they would have called it something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC from the &quot;what we know&quot; wiki, &quot;Solar XP&quot; is so named because it's &quot;the highest of XP,&quot; not because of anything inherent to the Solar splat, and all splats are supposed to get something similar.<br /> <br /> One of the things people hated most in 2e was not just mechanical power differences but advancement differences. Other splats paid more XP per Charm, started with fewer Charms, etc. It feels excessive on top of their Charms already being weaker, and their narrative role already describing them as not equal to the Solars. Bringing back XP disparity would be a terrible idea up there with retaining formlock and the out-of-Aspect surcharge. And since XP is a total meta-concept, it's pretty much unfair on a metagame level to tell the player of a Lunar &quot;hey, your XP doesn't go as far as the Solar, because they're better/stronger/etc&quot; when there are already a ton of other ways to show Solars are stronger without short-changing someone the worth of their XP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T16:41:09-07:00","id":851440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851393-what-is-the-solar-advantage-in-3ed?p=851409#post851409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CCS and SCS aren't the be-all end-all. Nor are they required for more powerful Workings.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but Solars don't have an advantage over other Exalts in terms of their sorcerous power other than SCS, so until E5 they're no better than other Celestials at sorcery (save for having one of the better dice caps for their occult rolls), and until E3 they aren't even better than Terrestrials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T16:45:07-07:00","id":851442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851393-what-is-the-solar-advantage-in-3ed#post851393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">why the other Exalted would serve the Solars in the First Age if they were not particularly powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars are still the mightiest of the Exalted.<br /> <br /> Part of being so mighty entails not really having any areas that their form doesn't allow them to be very powerful at, and having means of being competitive and victorious against beings that are mightier than they are.<br /> <br /> You look at some of the other Exalted in terms of character concepts and methodologies towards certain goals, and there's always something that doesn't quite fit for them. That might be about the power of their Charms, or it might be in some other quality in how they function; a notable part of Alchemicals, for instance, is the need to place themselves in the hands of mortal technicians for their Charms to be switched around or their traits to be improved.<br /> <br /> That's an answer to the question of how, when all of the Exalted are swirled around in the melting pot of the Primordial War and the early First Age, and possibly the Time of Tumult, the Solars come out on top.<br /> <br /> For the question of why follow the Solars throughout the First Age?<br /> <br /> They're really good at running a civilization.<br /> <br /> Not to disregard the Terrestrial Exalted, but that they're the least powerful Exalted is generally accepted as a matter of course.<br /> <br /> So if we're considering other groups to run the show... how are the others really acting in the same zone?<br /> <br /> The matter of Solars as the Lawgivers of humanity is more complex and holistic than the Bureaucracy Ability, but it can be examined as a way of comparing how suited they all are in the area of running things.<br /> <br /> Solars apply Bureaucracy through the lens of glorious culture heroes, so they're really good at running things in complex and nuanced ways, aimed at things like getting projects through efficiently and making institutions adhere to a central thesis statement and the like.<br /> <br /> Sidereals interpret Bureaucracy through the lens of esoteric mystics dedicated to enforcing the plans of Heaven, so it affords them powers to do things like surgically eliminate problem individuals or issues, or strike down spirits who are contravening the Celestial Order.<br /> <br /> Lunars don't do Bureaucracy at all. That's now just a matter of them not having Ability Charms (although that helps); the Lunar image and structure doesn't really extend itself to the management and regulation of complex institutions. A Lunar, as an individual, might be involved in such a thing, maybe even apply some of their Charms in the course of it, but I don't think there are really Lunar Charms built around the concept.<br /> <br /> You might sometimes get an Exigent who'll be suited to the task of king of the universe, but Exigents come and go; I don't think you can really build something that lasts around the assumption that a particular type will be there to sustain it.<br /> <br /> Being a Lawgiver, a stand out figure who guides and preserves the entirety of human civilization, has more to it than just running things, but all of what that &quot;more to it&quot; entails is not just what Solars do, they are things that they excel at.<br /> <br /> You've also got to look at them in terms of characterization beyond their powers; as people who have been Chosen by particular kinds of gods. You might get a Lunar who, in a straight up duel, is capable of defeating a Solar warrior of approximately the same power. Read the description of the Dawn Caste and consider what kinds of people consistently get Chosen as them; whatever the merits of a given Lunar who eventually turns into a Full Moon Caste, are they necessarily people who are cut from the same cloth?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T16:55:10-07:00","id":851448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851393-what-is-the-solar-advantage-in-3ed?p=851422#post851422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC from the &quot;what we know&quot; wiki, &quot;Solar XP&quot; is so named because it's &quot;the highest of XP,&quot; not because of anything inherent to the Solar splat, and all splats are supposed to get something similar.<br /> <br /> One of the things people hated most in 2e was not just mechanical power differences but advancement differences. Other splats paid more XP per Charm, started with fewer Charms, etc. It feels excessive on top of their Charms already being weaker, and their narrative role already describing them as not equal to the Solars. Bringing back XP disparity would be a terrible idea up there with retaining formlock and the out-of-Aspect surcharge. And since XP is a total meta-concept, it's pretty much unfair on a metagame level to tell the player of a Lunar &quot;hey, your XP doesn't go as far as the Solar, because they're better/stronger/etc&quot; when there are already a ton of other ways to show Solars are stronger without short-changing someone the worth of their XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may not have been all that clear. I wasn't anticipating that other splats wouldn't get equivalents, just that they might have different restrictions on earning/spending it. Solar XP is <i>really</i> flexible, which might be an advantage not everyone has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T16:55:53-07:00","id":851449,"title":"","content":"The Solar Advantage is having high-competency in all fields. His charms, for the most part, will add more dice, more successes, remove more failures, reroll more non-successes, etc, compared to his peers. He has a better excellency, and though excellencies are the least efficient of all his charms, he has access to charms that can give him situational free excellencies, or in the case of Melee, highly incentivize and pay-back for going for a full excellency. Other splats will do better than the Solar in certain fields (Lunars being more durable, having better ox-bodies, having charms to snap-cast spells when they dismiss a form, Sidereals can do some crazy nonsense with TN changing), but the Solar has high competence in all fields, and in many, is unsurpassed when he pursues them to their absolute peak. <br /> <br /> Other splats will not have the Supernal. They will, from what Devs have said, have something that takes the role of the Supernal, but is not the Rocket to E5 At Chargen that Solars get. Thus, at Char-gen, Solars can access incredibly powerful end-game charms in their chosen field right off the bat. <br /> <br /> Supernals are absurdly powerful. Take a Brawl Solar for example. Rush your way to Orichalcum Fists of Battle, and you've created someone who, though incredibly monofocused, can sidestep any and all issues of soak and no longer cares about building up initiative, save as a buffer from being crashed. A Solar could, at E1, have the entirety of a Martial Arts already learned, giving him a powerful offense and defense in many cases, while now free to spend all future charms on diversifying. A Solar has early access to Essence-Upgrades in his Supernal, as well; whilst an effect that adds (essence) to soak-penetration, for example, still uses his true essence, there are many charms that simply just get automatically better at essence breakpoints. <br /> <br /> To put this in a Fluff Perspective; a Dragonblooded Fire Aspect studies with the blade for decades. Alongside it, he learns the art of maneuvering courts, bending others to his will with words, leading men into battle, and otherwise expanding his repertoire of skills. At the age of 200, he could consider himself quite the grandmaster with a blade. Few Dragonblooded could be considered his peers in the field of battle when he pulls his jade sword from its sheathe.<br /> <br /> A freshly made Dawn matches him blow for blow, and even exceeds his talent. Though the Dawn has none of his oratory prowess, knowledge of war and strategy, or even his fiery speed as they leap from tree to tree and fight from shore to shore, a cold sweat beads on the back of his neck as he realizes this fresh-made stripling is BETTER than him with the sword, with only months of practice, where he's been swinging his sword for two centuries. And if he let the Solar age and diversify...too terrifying to think of. Best kill them now. But then the new Solar emerges from Exaltation as one of the greatest Archers in living memory. Or able to flick their wrist and bury a hundred knives in a hundred throats. Or finding their mind near-bursting with perfect battle-plans and stratagems, able to turn peasant rabble into the best mortal soldiers possible in weeks. <br /> <br /> And that's why Solars are scary. With Supernals in play, they enter the scene able to compete with elders in a single field of their choosing. Yes, they don't have the motepool to last in an endurance match. Yes, they won't have the breadth of ability and a library of charms large enough to answer every situation. But that Presence-Focused Zenith could turn a city against you in the week of his Exaltation. The Night will be harder to find than a single grain of sand in the desert as she slips through your home and steals your secret. Their Eclipse will spend days in the courts and know every single persons secrets, motivations, and desires. Their Twilight will already be able to craft rare wonders the world hasn't seen in millenia as if it were as natural as their own breathing. And they will cover each others weaknesses. And they'll only get stronger and shore up more of their weaknesses in time. <br /> <br /> Supernals are NOT a dubious advantage. Beyond the sheer strength of the Solar charm-library, it's arguably their most powerful current ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","name":"Grindavikur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T17:12:51-07:00","id":851458,"title":"","content":"I think another, simpler way of looking at it is: Solars have Ability Charms that are dedicated to being really good at those Abilities. Sidereals have Ability Charms that are dedicated to being really good at evoking a set of obscure parables. There are some really impressive Charms amidst that group, and have all kinds of significant circumstantial uses, but in a situation where you're all about wanting to be really good at running things or knowing things or investigating things, well... a Sidereal may or may not be out of their depth (although one of the advantages they can cultivate is being able to foresee and avoid situations in which they'll be out of their depth, so it doesn't necessarily hurt them in a way that would interfere with what they're made for). Hell, even something as simple as not being hit by things... Sidereals probably won't have exactly the same Dodge Charms as in First Edition, but if we're analysing in terms of principles then you could find something in the idea that a Sidereal who wants to stay in a fight and not get hit in the fight and is <i>good at dodging</i> has Duck Fate and not much else (and if that Charm is anything like the former perfect defences of the Solars, it can't exactly be used with impunity). Think about that; Dodge is designated in the corebook as an Ability important to combat, so what differences in heroes in combat do you suppose the difference in the Solar Dodge cascade and somebody relying on Absence and Duck Fate produces? None of that undermines the power of Avoidance Kata or Neighbourhood Relocation Scheme, but that doesn't make it a context in which they're relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T17:14:22-07:00","id":851460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grindavikur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851393-what-is-the-solar-advantage-in-3ed?p=851449#post851449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other splats will not have the Supernal. They will, from what Devs have said, have something that takes the role of the Supernal, but is not the Rocket to E5 At Chargen that Solars get. Thus, at Char-gen, Solars can access incredibly powerful end-game charms in their chosen field right off the bat.<br /> <br /> Supernals are NOT a dubious advantage. Beyond the sheer strength of the Solar charm-library, it's arguably their most powerful current ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Friendly reminder that the true power of Supernal is not having the endgame-style E5 Charms at chargen/E1, but having efficient, workhorse E3 Charms at chargen/E1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851393-what-is-the-solar-advantage-in-3ed?p=851440#post851440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but Solars don't have an advantage over other Exalts in terms of their sorcerous power other than SCS, so until E5 they're no better than other Celestials at sorcery (save for having one of the better dice caps for their occult rolls), and until E3 they aren't even better than Terrestrials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for their native Charms that improve their ability to do workings?<br /> <br /> Granted, they're no Fateful Excellency, but what is :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T17:21:43-07:00","id":851462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851393-what-is-the-solar-advantage-in-3ed?p=851460#post851460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Friendly reminder that the true power of Supernal is not having the endgame-style E5 Charms at chargen/E1, but having efficient, workhorse E3 Charms at chargen/E1.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, absolutely; most charms follow the rule of E2 and E3 being the real workhorses, with E4 and E5 being narrower/effects to expensive to use often, save for weird outliers like Resistance (I'm looking at you, Aegis of Invincible Might). Someone who's used their Supernal War to grab all of Wars E3 suite is incredibly strong, even though War has no E4/E5 charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","name":"Grindavikur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T18:18:47-07:00","id":851498,"title":"","content":"Actually the devs have said that other splats won't get anything like supernal. I believe they last said that their charmsets would be designed with that in mind. I presume that means really bottom loaded. Either way though, that's not really what gives Solars supremacy. What gives them supremacy is...everything. It's not really a mechanical thing, but in as far as it can be described mechanically they advance faster, and and easier, hit harder AND more efficiently. When they practice martial arts only sidereals, through esoteric means and great effort, can even attempt what Solars do without thinking.<br /> <br /> Not only do they have the highest limits but they've got lots of ways of pushing themselves beyond even that, see non-charm dice, for example. <br /> <br /> Also for what it's worth in my last campaign my dawn player and I figured out that he could solo kill 5 essence 5 immaculates with full artifact armor and weapons in a single turn before he took damage. He had to get a little bit lucky, but I really do mean a little bit, he basically had to roll within 10% of average for 2 rolls or something like that, otherwise the rolls were pretty solidly in his favour. And this campaign one of my dawns can pretty handily take a legion of 5,000 men and up to around 3 DB commanders all at once. Once you get into the territory of 5,000 men and 5 DB commanders his chances slip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T18:19:25-07:00","id":851500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851393-what-is-the-solar-advantage-in-3ed?p=851460#post851460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except for their native Charms that improve their ability to do workings?</div> </div> </div> </div>What native charms that improve their ability to do workings? There are no occult charms that give double Xs, non-charm dice or successes or otherwise allow you to break your dice cap, and as far as I recall the only non-occult charm that would aid in a working is Fate-Shifting Solar Arete, which we know is getting hit with a nerf hammer specifically to prevent it from boosting your working/crafting/etc rolls like it does right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T18:29:46-07:00","id":851504,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was misremembering.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851393-what-is-the-solar-advantage-in-3ed?p=851498#post851498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also for what it's worth in my last campaign my dawn player and I figured out that he could solo kill 5 essence 5 immaculates with full artifact armor and weapons in a single turn before he took damage. He had to get a little bit lucky, but I really do mean a little bit, he basically had to roll within 10% of average for 2 rolls or something like that, otherwise the rolls were pretty solidly in his favour. And this campaign one of my dawns can pretty handily take a legion of 5,000 men and up to around 3 DB commanders all at once. Once you get into the territory of 5,000 men and 5 DB commanders his chances slip.</div> </div> </div> </div>...........frankly, ugh","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T18:33:35-07:00","id":851506,"title":"","content":"The Solar advantagage is having the most powerful and direct charms.<br /> <br /> Don't see why they need anything else, tbh.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, the whole &quot;Lunars are as good as Solars in combat&quot; isn't a fluff thing, it's just a matter of how the Lunar book was written in 2nd ed. Their combat charms were more powerful than their social charms, and way more than their mental charms. Lunars were supposed to generally have charms that were slightly weaker, but they weren't really well-balanced against each other.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T22:00:14-07:00","id":851585,"title":"","content":"It's difficult to overstate what a huge effect Supernal and the generally high-end loadout Solars get at chargen has. Solars break the entire concept of what a young Exalt looks like, <i>and</i> they have the highest power level at maturity. If I were a member of the establishment factions, my superior preparation and infrastructure would not do much to make that less scary. The aforementioned combat-specced Full Moon, who is accustomed to running roughshod over everything he meets in direct combat, is not going to take much comfort in the knowledge that he has a <i>good shot</i> at beating a combat-specced Dawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 03-23-2016, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T22:08:29-07:00","id":851587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851393-what-is-the-solar-advantage-in-3ed?p=851585#post851585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's difficult to overstate what a huge effect Supernal and the generally high-end loadout Solars get at chargen has. Solars break the entire concept of what a young Exalt looks like, <i>and</i> they have the highest power level at maturity. If I were a member of the establishment factions, my superior preparation and infrastructure would not do much to make that less scary. The aforementioned combat-specced Full Moon, who is accustomed to running roughshod over everything he meets in direct combat, is not going to take much comfort in the knowledge that he has a <i>good shot</i> at beating a combat-specced Dawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is my problem with the new &quot;charms are not actually things&quot; approach, if charms are not things that an exalt does consciously, then how do you demonstrate an elder exalt being caught off guard? Also how aware of Supernals and Solar lore are the other factions in 3ed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T22:56:29-07:00","id":851599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851393-what-is-the-solar-advantage-in-3ed?p=851587#post851587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is my problem with the new &quot;charms are not actually things&quot; approach, if charms are not things that an exalt does consciously, then how do you demonstrate an elder exalt being caught off guard?</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I think of it is like this. There is no set thing for charms beyond application of essence to acquire a desired outcome. So every exalt sort of has their own way to come up with the result. So using solar saber, or what have you, might for one involve a sort of mental forging process to recreate a blade out of essence; another might require them to create a mold in their mind and fill it with essence; a third might just be tracing the pattern of a blade that exists somewhere in the world with their essence so the blade is basically an energy rubbing of a sword. The process would end up being what is referred to as a charm and the process is somewhat categorized in an exalts mind to make it easier and faster to think through and control the process as opposed to just hoping your instincts pull it off right.<br /> <br /> As for catching an elder off guard, I see no reason why that wouldn't be the same as any other person. I mean not every elder is going to invest in awareness charms, and there will almost always be points where an elder is not paying as much attention as they should or is distracted by something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851393-what-is-the-solar-advantage-in-3ed?p=851587#post851587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also how aware of Supernals and Solar lore are the other factions in 3ed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine there will probably be bits on how some Solars are unnaturally gifted or puissant with manifesting their power in certain ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 03-23-2016, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T01:04:41-07:00","id":851622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851393-what-is-the-solar-advantage-in-3ed?p=851506#post851506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Solar advantagage is having the most powerful and direct charms.<br /> <br /> Don't see why they need anything else, tbh.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, the whole &quot;Lunars are as good as Solars in combat&quot; isn't a fluff thing, it's just a matter of how the Lunar book was written in 2nd ed. Their combat charms were more powerful than their social charms, and way more than their mental charms. Lunars were supposed to generally have charms that were slightly weaker, but they weren't really well-balanced against each other.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They still got mulched as soon as Solars hit E4 and Infinite Mastery got into the picture, tho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T01:44:04-07:00","id":851629,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Supernals are basically the big thing that makes them a threat- they are masters at something out of the gate. The Dawn super combat then diversify strategy is probably one of the more dangerous Solars out there because they are one of the ones more likely to survive in a straight fight and only get more powerful as they round out their weaknesses. they have a strong early game and can diversify to get a solid late game<br /> <br /> The Nights are another harder threat that is most likely to survive early game, because they can probably hide so well, that they can just lay low until they do enough shenanigans to get into power without anyone knowing and when they are in a position of power, start shoring up their combat weaknesses for the late game.<br /> <br /> The Zeniths and Eclipses are terrifying in the long term, because while they are the ones more likely to get killed in the early game, if they make enough friends they can start building empires and organizations far better than a Dawn or Night even though those two are better at the early game survival, Zeniths and Eclipses are great late game powerhouses.<br /> <br /> Twilights are the ones most likely to die in the short term due to not having the ability to hide, the social connections or the fight abilities of the other Castes, but in the late game they are even more terrifying than the Zeniths and Eclipses due to their ability to call down cataclysms through Lore or Sorcery, make spirits do what they want, find out any secret, and create anything they need. <br /> <br /> and even then, the ones with Weak Early Games are the brainier Castes, who just need clever people to do them right to survive with the Supernals given to them- a Twilight with the ability to predict your hometown being destroyed is not someone you want to tick off, even in the Early Game, they just have to prove that they can do that. its just that Dawns and Nights are easier to succeed in the early game to survive to the late game, because the applications of their skills of how to do so are the most obvious. but all of them pose long term threats by simply having one Supernal ability that they can exploit to survive as long they can to really get going when they have enough experience and power to have a wide range of answers to what you can throw at them.<br /> <br /> I know that I'm probably going to be playing Dawns with a combat ability Supernal and Occult 5, because that combination means I'll get both a short term skill that will make sure I can probably defeat anyone in combat, and if I get to Essence 5,I'll be able to learn all of Sorcery to truly destroy my foes with demons and powerful spells while getting other utilities like transportation. Pairing up Supernals with Favored abilities that synergize well is important- if your Supernal skill is short term, select long term ones to grow into, if your supernal skill is a long term one, select short term skills to make sure you survive to use it effectively. <br /> <br /> but yeah, basically? Supernals are scary, whether long term or short term in their effects, and smart Solars know how to use what they are good at to get through the challenges they face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T03:23:49-07:00","id":851644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851393-what-is-the-solar-advantage-in-3ed?p=851622#post851622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> They still got mulched as soon as Solars hit E4 and Infinite Mastery got into the picture, tho.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I found that their own combat prowess suddenly increased massively at Essence 4, since with Moonsilver Carapace they were having 30 soak and hardness every round.<br /> Certainly, the two hardest characters by far in my game were the two Essence 4 Full Moons.<br /> <br /> It got nerfed hard in 2.5 though. At that point, suddenly the Zenith with Infinite Melee Mastery beat the Full Moon in a friendly staff duel, and everyone teased the Full Moon about it for months (not that he was fighting seriously).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T03:58:41-07:00","id":851649,"title":"","content":"I find descriptions of what makes Solars powerful do not adaquately describe why they ruled most of the First Age and have the potential to renew the world at the end of the Second. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">if charms are not things that an exalt does consciously, then how do you demonstrate an elder exalt being caught off guard</div> </div> </div> </div> Fighting is a thing that needs to be done consciously. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">how aware of Supernals</div> </div> </div> </div> They'll recognise the matter of Solars being able to achieve particularly iconic feats of their trademark skills without decades of refining their Essence. They just won't articulate that in terms of &quot;can buy Charms above their Essence score&quot;. Incidentally, how many people are blowing large chunks of their starting package to expand vertically as quickly as possible? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar lore</div> </div> </div> </div> Not sure what you mean by this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T06:58:23-07:00","id":851718,"title":"","content":"The only thing actually stopping a renewal of Creation As-Is is the Sids, Lunars, and Dragonblooded not working together. Between the three of them, they have more than enough combined power to wreck the threats to Creation, obliterate Shadowlands, bully the Abyssals for their lunch money, and noogie the Infernals hair right off. But they would, without the return of the Solars, never have the impetus to sit down and do some peace-talks. Solars returning breaks the stalemate and have the potential to move the setting towards peace between factions.<br /> <br /> Without the Solars, they could fix Creation if they'd just talk, kiss, and make up. With the Solars, they can do that, and also expand Creation back to the size it once was. <br /> <br /> As for the First Age, having appreciably but not overwhelmingly higher power than their kin, combined with very good bureaucratic/organization leadership abilities, and straightforward competence in all fields, means the Solars were a pretty good fit for the manager/leader role. That, and Conkers Bad Sunburn saying they were his Chosen probably helped a bunch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","name":"Grindavikur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T08:40:39-07:00","id":851779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851393-what-is-the-solar-advantage-in-3ed?p=851599#post851599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I think of it is like this. There is no set thing for charms beyond application of essence to acquire a desired outcome. So every exalt sort of has their own way to come up with the result. So using solar saber, or what have you, might for one involve a sort of mental forging process to recreate a blade out of essence; another might require them to create a mold in their mind and fill it with essence; a third might just be tracing the pattern of a blade that exists somewhere in the world with their essence so the blade is basically an energy rubbing of a sword. The process would end up being what is referred to as a charm and the process is somewhat categorized in an exalts mind to make it easier and faster to think through and control the process as opposed to just hoping your instincts pull it off right.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also seems worth noting that &quot;Charms not being things&quot; is likely to apply to the Solars more strongly than the other Exalt types.<br /> <br /> The other Exalt types have continuity of society and training, in some cases stretching back all the way to the First Age without significant disruption or interruption. Those guys are more likely to have had various savants and sifus actually try and sit down and unriddle their essence, if only to develop more effective training techniques. To an extent, the Exaltations will defy this, because they're miracles, but to an extent they <i>won't</i>, because the power they grant is somewhat uniform in nature. Amongst the non-Alchemicals, who are a special case, the Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals seem most likely to refer to what they do with their essence as &quot;Charms&quot; simply because that's likely to be the terminology they were taught by their training masters, who are drawing on thousands of years of tradition and codification of how they apply their essence to doing stuff.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T08:44:10-07:00","id":851783,"title":"","content":"Years from now, when the various non-Solar splats have been released, I'll find this thread odd to read up on.<br /> <br /> We're all sort of bullshitting here. I have no idea what the combat prowess of a 3rd Edition Lunar is compared to a 3rd Edition Solar. I have no idea how SMAs, astrology, and Sidereal charms compares to what Solars get.<br /> <br /> For all I know, a combat-centered Lunar can puree a combat-centered Solar, or at least they're designed to stand toe-to-toe from E1 to E5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T08:54:27-07:00","id":851800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851393-what-is-the-solar-advantage-in-3ed?p=851783#post851783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Years from now, when the various non-Solar splats have been released, I'll find this thread odd to read up on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your confidence there won't be a forumpocalypse sometime in that timeframe warms the cockles of my heart.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T13:44:23-07:00","id":851985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851393-what-is-the-solar-advantage-in-3ed?p=851458#post851458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think another, simpler way of looking at it is: Solars have Ability Charms that are dedicated to being really good at those Abilities. Sidereals have Ability Charms that are dedicated to being really good at evoking a set of obscure parables. There are some really impressive Charms amidst that group, and have all kinds of significant circumstantial uses, but in a situation where you're all about wanting to be really good at running things or knowing things or investigating things, well... a Sidereal may or may not be out of their depth (although one of the advantages they can cultivate is being able to foresee and avoid situations in which they'll be out of their depth, so it doesn't necessarily hurt them in a way that would interfere with what they're made for).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's plausible some of it probably does work that way. Solars simply have a nature or design that is more efficient and generally applicable to abilities (which pretty much define the heroic actions that are the focus of the game) and more ability to focus their power, and this simply makes them mightier.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if it *all* worked that way, or to a very large degree, then Jenna M wouldn't have had to worry about or consider things like &quot;Is this Charm less efficient than Hungry Tiger Technique?&quot; (which she did) when developing the Sidereals, as the appropriate power and style levels would've just naturally fallen out of the process. By which I mean she *was* specifically designing Sidereals to lack or be weak in particular capabilities and to have certain gaps - it wasn't just a natural consequence of designing them towards their paradigm. What would've happened if she hadn't made those considerations during design....<br /> <br /> I don't think we'll ever, really, know what would happen, which set of heroes would end up being the most efficient and capable at achieving their goals, assuming the designers were shooting for an equalish sort of degree of power and capability - either an Infernals like design, a Sidereals like design, a Dragonblooded like design, a Solars like design, etc. - as for one that's simply not on Exalted's design agenda to test and for another, even if implemented, testing what &quot;works best&quot; would depend incredibly on the ingenuity of players and their choices and imagination in defining and working towards their characters' goals (some of which goals would be incommensurable between the different designs).<br /> <br /> I'm a bit ideological on this though - I think it's a better way to look at Exalted as a whole that the Solars' power is frankly sort of arbitrary, and contingent on the history and in particular their patron setting himself up as the biggest overgod in slightly questionable circumstances (in which, in case this seems anti-UCS, all the Incarna share), and that Solar strength doesn't derive as a natural consequence of the style and form of their Charms and Castes. (And so, as we all do, I prefer to believe in a version of reality that conforms to what I'd like to be true!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T15:15:07-07:00","id":852044,"title":"","content":"Based primarily on viewing Mastery vs normal charm levels, I'd say that charm for charm, it looks like the intended paradigm is that Solars get a small advantage in every single charm, which overall works out to a giant advantage in any category they invest in. Every Solar charm gives them a slight advantage where immediately comparable [this assumes the others have a comparable charm and aren't trapped behind esoterica for Sidereals or &quot;That's not an Attribute task&quot; for Lunars in the given situation], and the more charms that factor in, the more opportunities the Solar has to shine above the others.<br /> <br /> It's not the 2e &quot;One Solar charm is worth FIVE Lunar charms in any noncombat category&quot;, but Solars start slightly ahead at any given task, usually have charms more directly applicable to that task, and get a continual increase in overall capability.. Which couples with a dicecap for their excellencies that is always at the maximum possible value -you don't have to cleverly think how to stunt STRONGLY hearing the guy to get that +10 dice [Str 5 Per 5] on excellency, you just have +10 dice because that's your jam yo.<br /> <br /> I may be wildly proven wrong in the future, but I'm hopeful this is accurate; a combination of like 20% &quot;Lunars/Sidereals don't really do things that direct way&quot; with 80% &quot;Your charms aren't half their power, but they're not exactly equal either&quot;.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, and of course Supernal and its' &quot;This power! How can a swordsman be THAT STRONG?!&quot; effect, assuming Lunars and Sidereals don't get a similar toy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 03-23-2016, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T15:40:11-07:00","id":852063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grindavikur</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars returning breaks the stalemate and have the potential to move the setting towards peace between factions.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's more to the Solar Exalted than just intruding on the status quo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T15:48:27-07:00","id":852075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851393-what-is-the-solar-advantage-in-3ed?p=852063#post852063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's more to the Solar Exalted than just intruding on the status quo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutely! I've talked about it in other posts in this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","name":"Grindavikur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T15:49:18-07:00","id":852076,"title":"","content":"I think there's also something assumed where Solars were kind of just tangental to the infrastructure that was the First Age. To some extent,t hey actually were. No one else likely has something like the ability to rest things from the Wyld like a Solar might, nor can anyone do Solar Circle magic and some of the Workings involved. You also likey have some areas in Artifice unique to Solar insights and skill with the art (represented by how one would go about using Words-As-Workshops Wisdom to do Weird Shit).<br /> <br /> The current Age is a result of more than just political bickering. Solars disappearing did a big number on the world's infrastructure. Additionally, the Lunar Exalted of the Time of Tumult as I gather are just fundementally another sort of thing from what they were in the First Age. We don't have some situation that the solution is to go all and try to rebuild the First Age like it was before. Not only do the Solars not have the historical momentum or mandate to do so, but good chunks of the potential players (including many Solar Exaltations) are simply not what they were before to do such with anyhow.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T16:09:19-07:00","id":852088,"title":"","content":"In terms of being able to maintain the Defense of Creation indefinitely, and restore the magic and techne of the First Age, I'm not sure the Sidereals, Lunars and Dragonblooded could get close, without the genius of the Solar Exalted. Possibly not without enough seriously risky, bravura, seat-of-their-pants Sorcerous Workings and dealings with strange entities that, statistically, something is seriously likely to go wrong at some point. <br /> <br /> (Although equally, perhaps much is possible with magical research, with enough time and effort.)<br /> <br /> But can they harness energy, medicine, economics and principles of government and justice such that a pretty large population of humans could live what we today would consider to be a &quot;good life&quot;? I think they could. (If only until the Deathlords or Fair Folk got &quot;lucky once&quot;.) I'm pretty comfortable with thinking of this as a pretty distinct goal from restoring the grandeur of the First Age.<br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> Another thing I suppose I thought of, in a meta way, is lot of the Solar strength as well, in practical terms, in any given game, is in the story of that game complying with their genre.<br /> <br /> It's pretty easy to imagine stories where you *need* greater than human specifically bureaucratic wisdom and talent to set your society on the right path.<br /> <br /> It's also pretty easy to imagine stories where, actually, that's totally superfluous, because talented human people are pretty much good enough at bureaucracy as it stands to do anything they need to do with it, and what would be a lot more useful would be adding to that a very flexible person with lot of animal power and a general superiority of intelligence, cunning and imagination, who uses that in the right place at the right time.<br /> <br /> Being smart people, it's pretty easy for us to imagine both.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut a lot of what Exalted does, is by the way it talks it gets us complying with its own assumptions, in which the first is *probably* much more generally the case. So, the power of the Solars is to solve the problems that are set up by the assumptions of much of the fluff in the books (that you need people with specific kinds of talent the Solars have), even if those are not actually necessarily general to reality or stories in any way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T16:18:17-07:00","id":852097,"title":"","content":"To take a new tack: The Solars have great potential to change things and be leaders because they also tend to be the &quot;best&quot; of what humanity has to offer. I am simplifying immensely but:<br /> <br /> -Dragonblooded are born into their power, and even if they have to earn it, it is tied up in a quality that mortals do not possess and cannot gain.<br /> -Sidereals are destined to Exalt, regardless of what they do and their entire life is built around moving them toward that.<br /> -Lunars draw on the archetypes of the monster, the outsiders, the wild. They are individualistic without being notably inspiring.<br /> -Solars are basically cultural heroes from the ground up. They are walking lessons in what human excellence can accomplish and how humans should use their power. (occassionaly by being negative examples.)<br /> <br /> <br /> When a mortal sees a Solar swordsman standing unmarked against a dozen foes the takeaway isn't &quot;This is a horrible monster or half-divine bloodline that I cannot be part of&quot; its &quot;This is what I could do if I REALLY applied myself and leveraged all my talent and focus.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now of course this mortal can't actually do that, but by developing themselves in that way they can reach their actual potential. This ties in to the notion that Solar 'magic&quot; is human excellence writ large rather than esoteric power. The Twilight is not conjuring little gods to build things for them, they are just that good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T16:48:10-07:00","id":852112,"title":"","content":"Inspiration's an odd thing. A lot of people might find animals more inspiring than other people, even if that person's someone they can aspire to and the animal isn't. Does the grace of the eagle speak to you more about what you should aspire to be? For all that you can never be an eagle. Maybe it does. (And do people find inspiring generally only what they can aspire to become? Does Jesus not inspire many religious Christians, even though they cannot actually aspire to be the Son of God? Does Ahlat inspire the people of Harbourhead, even though he is a god and they can never really be?).<br /> <br /> Irregardless, you're right that Solars are *intended* to embody inspiration though, from the text, straight from the 1e core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T16:40:51-07:00","id":856073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851393-what-is-the-solar-advantage-in-3ed?p=852112#post852112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inspiration's an odd thing. A lot of people might find animals more inspiring than other people, even if that person's someone they can aspire to and the animal isn't. Does the grace of the eagle speak to you more about what you should aspire to be? For all that you can never be an eagle. Maybe it does. (And do people find inspiring generally only what they can aspire to become? Does Jesus not inspire many religious Christians, even though they cannot actually aspire to be the Son of God? Does Ahlat inspire the people of Harbourhead, even though he is a god and they can never really be?).<br /> <br /> Regardless, you're right that Solars are *intended* to embody inspiration though, from the text, straight from the 1e core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually imitation of Christ is a think Christians are often encouraged to do and many books have been written to that effect. They will fall short but are supposed to become better people for the attempt and continuing effort.<br /> <br /> Solars do have a slight edge in inspiration in that their excellence is of the same sort that humans can accomplish. A swordsman can get more direct examples for his own techniques by watching Solar melee charms than Lunar strength charms simply by virtue of the Solar's charms are examples of really good swordsmanship while the Lunars are examples of being really strong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}